These graphs illustrate the behavior of the remaining inverse trigonometric functions. The inverse cotangent function is defined for all real numbers, while the inverse secant and cosecant functions are defined for $x$ values less than or equal to $-1$ and greater than or equal to $1$. The ranges of these functions are restricted to ensure they are one-to-one, which is necessary for them to have inverses.

